// Myna macOS Designated Requirement (DR) — explicit, pinned, and NEVER to be
// changed once a signed build has shipped and users have granted TCC
// permissions (microphone / kTCCServiceAudioCapture) against it.
//
// Background (see docs/releasing-macos.md and Apple TN3127):
//   - macOS records an app's DR against every privacy grant it holds. If a
//     later build's DR does not match, the grant is silently denied with no
//     re-prompt.
//   - Ad-hoc signing (no certificate) produces a DR that is a bare `cdhash`,
//     which is different on every rebuild — so ad-hoc builds can never keep
//     a stable TCC grant across updates.
//   - Signing with a certificate (even an untrusted/self-issued one — trust
//     is irrelevant to requirement evaluation unless the expression itself
//     contains `anchor trusted`) lets the DR name the certificate's team
//     instead of a per-build hash, which *is* stable across rebuilds.
//   - The *default* DR that codesign derives from an Apple Development
//     identity pins `leaf[subject.CN]`, whose value can change on
//     certificate renewal. Pinning `leaf[subject.OU]` (the stable Team ID)
//     instead avoids that churn — but only if we set it explicitly, once,
//     and never again.
//
// `__APPLE_TEAM_ID__` is substituted by scripts/release-macos.sh from the
// `APPLE_TEAM_ID` environment variable at build time. This file is a
// template — it is never used verbatim as a requirement source, and the
// Team ID is intentionally not hardcoded here (this repo is public).
anchor apple generic and certificate leaf[subject.OU] = "__APPLE_TEAM_ID__"
